From 07e570b3b9fcf197a084984a4e9d642fcb8d7966 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grubbychicken <ben@grbychkn.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prefill sparse attention: same bits in shapes that keep more
 gathers in flight (28K: 525 -> 577 tok/s)

- normalize_h: normalize's arithmetic, the probabilities rounded to half in place (sparse_pv rounded them on load)
- sparse_pv_h: 256 context columns x 32 staged keys a CTA (GR8_PF_SPV, default 4; each probability row read twice,
  not 8 times): values 6.12 -> 3.94 s over 1,152 sparse calls at 28K
- sparse_qk_v: 128 keys x 32 staged dims a CTA (GR8_PF_SQK, default 1): scores 4.85 -> 3.96 s
- GR8_PF_USTAT: diagnostic stage timing and the distinct keys of 16 / 32 / 64-row blocks (the union a block-shared
  attention would read: 5.9K / 7.5K / 9.4K at 20-28K context, 2.9-4.6x the 2048 a row)
Every output element keeps its operands and accumulation order: offline 28K step lines and 200 generated tokens identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
