 | `GR8_PF_STAGGER` | int | `0` |  | Lane B's prefill stream first sleeps this many microseconds, so its first work starts after lane A's. Writes nothing. |
 | `GR8_PF_STRIPE_MIN` | int | `1048576` | 8192.. | With GR8_PF_STRIPE=1, the smallest prefill payload write in bytes that goes out split over the two rails. |
+| `GR8_PF_USTAT` | flag | `0` | 0\|1 | Diagnostic: times each prefill attention stage (CUDA events, dense and sparse totals printed every 432 calls) and after each call counts the distinct keys the selections of blocks of 16, 32 and 64 consecutive rows cover (the keys a block-shared attention would read). Synchronizes. |
